    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d713">

                <pb facs="0873" n="749" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg749"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.51/621</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Representative on Special Mission in Cuba</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Crowder</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-10-20"><hi rendition="#italic">October 20,
                        1921</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received October 24.]</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: Under date of October 17th,
                    I transmitted a translation of President Zayas’ reply to my letter of October
                    10th, remarking in the letter of transmittal<anchor n="63" xml:id="d713-f1"/>
                    that I was retaining the Spanish original here but that a literal copy of the
                    same would be forwarded in due course.</p>
                <p>Having regard to the confidential character of this letter and its great
                    importance, I have decided to send the original to the Department and retain
                    here the copy.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. H. Crowder</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d713-a1.xml" xpointer="d713-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
